From dfa7edce78e6f68ea1f55c848682230546a1e783 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 15:55:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 248/638] base: add AROS child launch lifecycle probe
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model

AI_STATUS: hosted-validated, native-pending

ROOT_CAUSE: The new AROS LaunchProcess implementation lacked a focused executable proving argument quoting, distinct process identity, concurrent lifetime, exit propagation, and WaitForExit behavior independently of Chromium child-role plumbing.

FIX_REASON: Add an AROS-only probe that launches itself with difficult arguments, validates them in the child, remains visible as a separate process, exits with a sentinel status, and verifies that status in the parent.

SCOPE: base/test/BUILD.gn and base/test/launch_process_aros_probe.cc only.

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-windowed launch_process_aros_probe passed. Clean hosted AROS observed parent 35 and child 36, exact argv validation, child exit 23, parent WaitForExit success, and probe return 0. Evidence: /home/terminills/Documents/GitHub/chromium-aros/test-artifacts/hosted-20260716-process-model. Native SMP replay is.

RISK: low. Test-only AROS target; native validation remains pending.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap,,
---
 base/test/BUILD.gn                     |   8 ++
 base/test/launch_process_aros_probe.cc | 108 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 116 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 base/test/launch_process_aros_probe.cc

